ty and sustainability challenges into opportunities for customers in more than 110 countries. UL Solutions delivers testing, inspection and certification services, together with software products and advisory offerings, that support our customers’ product innovation and business growth. The UL Mark serves as a recognized symbol of trust in our customers’ products and reflects an unwavering commitment to advancing our safety mission. We help our customers innovate, launch new products and services, navigate global markets and complex supply chains, and grow sustainably and responsibly into the future. Our science is your advantage.\n   \n\n  \n\n**About The Team**\n We solve our customers’ problems. Within Software \\& Advisory (S\\&A) services, UL Solutions’ Enterprise Sustainability business focuses on solving some of the most pressing world challenges \\- renewables, energy transition, sustainability, health \\& wellbeing, return to work and people safety. We do this through Renewable Energy Advisory and Digital Services, Environmental, Health and Safety Software \\& Learning programs, best in class Sustainability and ESG reporting software with UL 360, advisory services, subject matter experts and Healthy Buildings testing and verification.","https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4427195823":"**About The Company**\n Appgate is a leading provider of security solutions dedicated to safeguarding organizations' most valuable assets through innovative technology and expert services. Specializing in high\\-performance Zero Trust Network Access (ZTNA) solutions and Cyber Advisory Services, Appgate offers unparalleled protection, seamless interoperability, and peak performance to enterprises and government agencies worldwide. The company’s commitment to security excellence is reflected in its unique approach to network security, emphasizing direct\\-routed ZTNA solutions that ensure robust protection without compromising on speed or user experience.\n   \n\n  \n\n As part of its ongoing growth and innovation, Appgate is expanding its platform to include a dedicated Data \\+ AI team. This initiative aims to develop next\\-generation security solutions leveraging advanced data engineering, AI\\-driven threat detection, network observability, insider risk monitoring, and the securing of emerging Agentic AI systems. Working at Appgate provides a rare opportunity to be part of a small, private, high\\-impact organization where your contributions directly influence the company's strategic direction, architecture, and core products shaping the future of security technology.\n   \n\n  \n\n**About The Role**\n We are seeking experienced Staff and Principal Engineers who excel in ambiguous environments, thrive on greenfield projects, and possess the technical leadership qualities necessary to serve as both architects and mentors. In this role, you will be instrumental in building the foundational data infrastructure, including large\\-scale data pipelines, cloud\\-native data lakes, and AI systems capable of operating across AWS cloud and on\\-premises environments. As a founding team engineer dedicated to this initiative, you will define the architecture, select the technology stack, and establish engineering standards for a new core capability within the company.\n   \n\n  \n\n Your work will enable AI\\-driven security capabilities such as network policy analysis, real\\-time network observability, root cause analysis through AI agents, threat anomaly detection, insider risk monitoring, and securing autonomous AI systems. This role offers the chance to shape the future of AI\\-powered security solutions, working closely with research and product teams to operationalize machine learning models, and influence the company's technical strategy.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Qualifications**\n* 8\\+ years of experience in software or data engineering roles\n* At least 3 years in a senior technical leadership position (Staff, Principal, or Architect level)\n* Hands\\-on experience building distributed data systems, including streaming, pipelines, ETL, batch, and real\\-time processing\n* Strong knowledge of cloud\\-native platforms such as AWS, GCP, or Azure\n* Proficiency with containerization and orchestration tools like Kubernetes\n* Experience with modern data technologies such as Kafka, Spark/Flink, Elastic Search, Redshift, Delta Lake, and dbt\n* Familiarity with AI/ML production workflows including feature stores, model deployment, and monitoring\n* Proven ability to lead greenfield initiatives, shape architecture, and mentor engineering teams\n* Experience within the security domain, including secure access, threat detection, and anomaly detection\n* Comfortable working in high\\-growth, ambiguous environments with minimal structure\n* Based in New York City and available to work onsite 3\\-4 days per week at One Penn Plaza\n\n\n**Responsibilities**\n* Design and implement scalable data pipelines, event streaming systems, and a centralized data lake to unify security data sources\n* Partner with AI researchers and product teams to operationalize machine learning and AI models on the data platform\n* Make foundational architecture decisions regarding tools, frameworks, and cloud infrastructure to ensure scalability, reliability, and compliance\n* Guide and mentor engineers, especially those newer to modern data engineering and AI practices, fostering a culture of innovation and excellence\n* Translate business goals into technical roadmaps by asking the right questions, identifying gaps, and driving clarity from ambiguity\n* Collaborate closely with the CTO and leadership to align the technical strategy with the company's vision for AI\\-driven security solutions\n\n\n**Benefits**\n* Competitive salary, bonus, and equity options\n* 401(k) plan with company match\n* Comprehensive medical, dental, and vision insurance\n* Short\\-term and long\\-term disability coverage, life insurance\n* Flexible time\\-off policy to promote work\\-life balance\n* Remote work options with a home office setup stipend\n* Mobile phone stipend for work convenience\n* Certification assistance program to support professional growth\n\n\n Equal Opportunity\n   \n\n  \n\n Appgate is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees and applicants. We do not discriminate based on race, color, religion, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic under applicable law. We welcome diverse perspectives and are dedicated to fostering a workplace where everyone can thrive.","https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4414522607":"**Job Number: R0240044**\n Data Scientist\n   \n\n  \n\n**The Opportunity** \n**:**\n As a data scientist, you’re excited at the prospect of unlocking the secrets held by a data set, and you’re fascinated by the possibilities presented by IoT, machine learning, and artificial intelligence. In an increasingly connected world, massive amounts of structured and unstructured data open new opportunities. As a Data Scientist at Booz Allen, you can help turn these complex data sets into useful information to solve global challenges. Across private and public sectors—from fraud detection to cancer research to national intelligence—we need you to help find the answers in the data.\n   \n\n  \n\n On our team, you’ll use your analytical skills and data science knowledge to create real\\-world impact. You’ll work closely with your clients to understand their questions and needs, and then dig into their data\\-rich environments to find the pieces of their information puzzle. You’ll develop algorithms and systems and use the right combination of tools and frameworks to turn sets of disparate data points into objective answers to help clients make informed decisions. Ultimately, you’ll provide a deep understanding of the data, what it all means, and how it can be used.\n   \n\n  \n\n Work with us as we use data science for good.\n   \n\n  \n\n Join us. The world can’t wait.\n   \n\n  \n\n**You Have:**\n* 2\\+ years of experience with data cleansing, analysis, visualization, API connections, or data mining\n* 2\\+ years of experience analyzing structured and unstructured data\n* 2\\+ years of experience working with Python, including leveraging several different libraries, such as Pandas or Numpy\n* Experience developing predictive data models, quantitative analyses, or natural language processing\n* Experience using cloud data tools within AWS, Azure, or Oracle\n* Experience with visualization packages, including Plotly, Seaborn, or ggplot2\n* Secret clearance\n* Bachelor’s degree\n\n\n**Nice If You Have:**\n* Experience with engineering AI solutions, including accessing Large Language Model (LLM) APIs, self\\-hosting LLMs, fine\\-tuning LLMs, or implementing Model Context Protocol\n* Experience working with the War Data Platform, USAF VAULT, or Palantir Foundry\n* Experience with distributed data and computing tools, including MapReduce, Hadoop, Hive, EMR, Kafka, Spark, Gurobi, or MySQL\n* Experience writing infrastructure\\-as\\-code leveraging Terraform or a similar tool\n* Experience working with DoW clients\n* Experience developing visually compelling PowerPoint decks and other products to support client delivery\n* Possession of excellent verbal and written communication skills\n* TS/SCI clearance\n\n\n**Clearance:**\n Applicants selected will be subject to a security investigation and may need to meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information; Secret clearance is required.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Compensation**\n At Booz Allen, we celebrate your contributions, provide you with opportunities and choices, and support your total well\\-being. Our offerings include health, life, disability, financial, and retirement benefits, as well as paid leave, professional development, tuition assistance, work\\-life programs, and dependent care. Our recognition awards program acknowledges employees for exceptional performance and superior demonstration of our values. Full\\-time and part\\-time employees working at least 20 hours a week on a regular basis are eligible to participate in Booz Allen’s benefit programs. Individuals that do not meet the threshold are only eligible for select offerings, not inclusive of health benefits. We encourage you to learn more about our total benefits by visiting the Resource page on our Careers site and reviewing Our Employee Benefits page.\n   \n\n  \n\n Salary at Booz Allen is determined by various factors, including but not limited to location, the individual’s particular combination of education, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience, as well as contract\\-specific affordability and organizational requirements. The projected compensation range for this position is $77,500\\.00 to $176,000\\.00 (annualized USD). The estimate displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is just one component of Booz Allen’s total compensation package for employees. This posting will close within 90 days from the Posting Date.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Identity Statement**\n As part of the hiring process, we will ask you to complete an identity verification process that leverages advanced biometrics and artificial intelligence to ensure authenticity and protect against identity fraud. You are expected to be on camera during interviews and assessments. We reserve the right to take your picture to verify your identity and prevent fraud.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Candidate AI Usage Policy**\n AI is a part of our daily work at Booz Allen, and we are committed to the responsible and ethical use of AI tools. However, we want to ensure a fair candidate process based on\n **your** \n own skills and knowledge. As part of this commitment, the use of artificial intelligence (AI) or other tools to assist with responses during interviews (whether in\\